			"text":"Leviticus",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-120,
			"y":350,
			"width":260,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"a509909892c4686f",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Exodus",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-120,
			"y":270,
			"width":260,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"c08d77e4229f4531",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Gen 11:5-7",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":980,
			"y":-700,
			"width":260,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"27143047079fe378",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"God",
			"styleAttributes":{"textAlign":"center"},
			"x":820,
			"y":-1940,
			"width":100,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"113ba0478d8330cc",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Used from Genesis 1:1 through 2:3",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":500,
			"y":-1820,
			"width":260,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"aad5c37af5c5f59d",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Gods",
			"styleAttributes":{"textAlign":"center"},
			"x":820,
			"y":-1820,
			"width":100,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"5d6c8586f6794699",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"-hebrew symbols-",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":500,
			"y":-1680,
			"width":260,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"913a1b6446d226ff",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Lord",
			"styleAttributes":{"textAlign":"center"},
			"x":820,
			"y":-1680,
			"width":100,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"48326292963a9e31",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Elohim is actually plural and most times ought to be translated as \"the gods\". We translate it as \"god\" most of the time, solely due to the Christian narrative of a monotheistic god being such a string influence over translation.",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":1040,
			"y":-2020,
			"width":460,
			"height":140
		},
		{
			"id":"9574ca36f7187ed0",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Psalm 82 is a good example of Elohim being translated both as god and the gods in the same sentence.",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":1040,
			"y":-1860,
			"width":420,
			"height":100
		},
		{
			"id":"4ddc402d66eecfaf",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"God (elohim) has taken his place in the divine council; in the midst of the gods (elohim) he holds judgment.",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":1040,
			"y":-1720,
			"width":420,
			"height":80
		},
		{
			"id":"a8ba4beb315d283e",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"God",
			"styleAttributes":{"textAlign":"center"},
			"x":820,
			"y":-1600,
			"width":100,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"235c4b1b7737b32e",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Introduced from Genesis 2:4",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":500,
			"y":-1560,
			"width":260,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"2ca02fafd09444e5",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Yahweh",
			"styleAttributes":{"textAlign":"center"},
			"x":820,
			"y":-1530,
			"width":100,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"5d97be36a53c0009",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Jehovah",
			"styleAttributes":{"textAlign":"center"},
			"x":820,
			"y":-1460,
			"width":100,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"a719481c268895af",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"-hebrew symbols-",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":500,
			"y":-1340,
			"width":180,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"3ba29e4299c6ece2",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"The tetragrammaton",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":760,
			"y":-1340,
			"width":260,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"ab408f61ba782b1b",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"The Beast of Revelation",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-120,
			"y":-2040,
			"width":260,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"fe2261e9c4975fa6",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"A physical person",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-120,
			"y":-1960,
			"width":260,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"bb1de6ece5476b72",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Never mentions having a son",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-120,
			"y":-1860,
			"width":260,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"87204bd797c102bb",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"The word God or Lord in the Bible is translated from several different words mainly, Elohim and YHWH. In this study we're going to use the transliteration of the actual Hebrew word that has been translated as God in the Garden of Eden story. That word is Yahweh.\n\nTransliteration means the English-sounding equivalent of the original work in the Hebrew.",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-120,
			"y":-1790,
			"width":420,
			"height":260
		},
		{
			"id":"d190ed7ab0311715",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Elohim",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":360,
			"y":-1700,
			"width":100,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"397d5e96d1822b29",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"YHWH",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":360,
			"y":-1520,
			"width":100,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"01bfd83da6aa749e",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"in the cool of the evening, the man and his wife **heard** the Lord God **walking** around in the garden.  So they hid from the Lord God amount the trees in the garden. \n\nThe Lord God called to the man and asked him, \"**Where are you**?\"  \n\nHe answered, \"**I heard you** in the garden. I was afraid because I was naked, so I **hid**.\"",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":400,
			"y":-1120,
			"width":520,
			"height":210
		},
		{
			"id":"d80d02703cf69bd9",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Genesis 3:8-10",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":980,
			"y":-1045,
			"width":180,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"9210fffad4d1e18a",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"The the Lord God said, \"The man has become **like one of us**, since he knows good and evil. He must not reach our and take the fruit from the tree of life and eat. Then he would live forever.\"",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":400,
			"y":-880,
			"width":520,
			"height":85
		},
		{
			"id":"5600df8545cd8287",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Genesis 3:22",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":980,
			"y":-865,
			"width":200,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"66a8de5d8adaa01d",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Babel",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":220,
			"y":-760,
			"width":110,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"41bab7c0db34d2e0",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"The Lord **came down to see** the city this is about the tower (of babel) that the descendants of Adam were building.  The Lord said, \"They are one people with one language. This is only the beginning of what they will do! Now nothing they plan to do will be too difficult for them. **Let us go down there** and mix up their language so that they won't understand each other.\"",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":400,
			"y":-760,
			"width":520,
			"height":170
		},
		{
			"id":"8e176b4b3bbc87ee",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"The Garden",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":200,
			"y":-1125,
			"width":130,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"18882ed6a2528d45",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Who is the God of this world/age?",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-120,
			"y":-1260,
			"width":300,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"49eb7e0884454a3b",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"According to the entirety of Torah, who is the God of this world?",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":240,
			"y":-1260,
			"width":300,
			"height":80
		},
		{
			"id":"0f4bdee6da82b4ab",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Yahweh",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":580,
			"y":-1240,
			"width":100,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"9019bcf4f163da47",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Genesis",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-120,
			"y":-1125,
			"width":260,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"4dc5c38664643691",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"The one who set that set himself up as god",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-120,
			"y":-2560,
			"width":380,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"8ea53b2b95df7a36",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"The one that tried to overthrow the kingdom",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-120,
			"y":-2460,
			"width":380,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"225ff2b0c38f2f6f",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"The individual behind Rome and their creation of the Christian myth",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-120,
			"y":-2360,
			"width":380,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"ee75d5d1a0e1d958",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"the god of this age; the god of this world",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-120,
			"y":-2280,
			"width":380,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"f8a61f3832e19d68",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"the adversary of humankind",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-120,
			"y":-2200,
			"width":260,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"429ef2bae519ad74",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Satan / the Devil",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-120,
			"y":-2120,
			"width":260,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"2703174326075d91",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"...am",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":220,
			"y":-570,
			"width":110,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"e5c3ec81095904e3",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"The Lord appeared to Abraham by the oak trees belonging to Mamre as he was sitting at the entrance of his tent during the hottest part of the day. Abraham looked up, and suddenly he saw **three men standing near him**. When he saw them, **he ran to meet them**, and he bowed with his face touching the ground.\n\n\"Please, sir,\" Abraham said, \"stop by to visit me for a while. Why don't we let someone bring a little water? **After you wash your feet you can stretch out and rest under the tree**. Let me bring you some bread that you can regain your strength. After that you can leave, since this is why you stopped by to visit me.\"\n\nThey answered, \"That's fine. Do as you say.\"",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":400,
			"y":-560,
			"width":560,
			"height":340
		},
		{
			"id":"9a7a6226598c72da",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"So Jacob was left alone then a man wrestled with him until dawn. When the man saw that he could not win against Jacob **he touched the socket of Jacob's hip** so that it was dislocated as they wrestled.\n\nThen the man said, \"**Let me go**; it's almost dawn.\" But Jacob answered, \"**I won't let you go** until you bless me.\"\nSo the man asked him, \"What's your name?\"\n\"Jacob,\" he answered.\nThe man said, \"Your name will no longer be Jacob but Israel \\[He Wrestles With God\\], because you have wrestled with God and with men - and you have won.\"\n\nSo Jacob named that place Peniel \\[Face of God\\], because he said, \"I **have seen God face to face**, but my life was saved.\"",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":400,
			"y":-200,
			"width":560,
			"height":360
		},
		{
			"id":"a42ec79438552ee6",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Genesis 35:9",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":400,
			"y":180,
			"width":260,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"f8e23aae764a48e5",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Genesis 26:2",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":220,
			"y":260,
			"width":185,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"6ed7b8479391fd60",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"As they left Pharaoh, they found Moses and Aaron waiting for them. So they said, \"May the Lord see what you have done and judge you! You have made Pharaoh and his officials hate us. You have given them an excuse to kill us.\"\n**Moses went back to the Lord** and asked, \"Why have you brought this trouble on your people? Why did you send me? Ever since I went to Pharaoh to speak for you, he had treated your people cruelly, and you have done nothing at all to rescue your people.\"",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":220,
			"y":360,
			"width":740,
			"height":180
		},
		{
			"id":"1f5c30c03fc56883",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"As soon as Modes went into the tent, the column of smoke would come down and stay at the entrance to the tent while the Lord spoke with Moses.\n\n**The Lord would speak to Moses personally, as a man speaks to his friend**. Then moses would come back to the camp, but his assistant, Joshua, son of Nun, stayed inside the tent.",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":220,
			"y":560,
			"width":740,
			"height":140
		},
		{
			"id":"9faeb379948f4481",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Exodus 33",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":1020,
			"y":600,
			"width":260,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"750a9d0d2ec7bf4a",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Chapters 1-7",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":220,
			"y":710,
			"width":260,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"a9bd77eb7f955069",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Suddenly, the Lord said to Moses, Aaron, and Miriam, \"All three of you come to the tent of meeting.\" So all three of them came. Then the Lord came down in the column of smoke and **stood at the entrance to the tent**. He called to Aaron and Miriam, and they both came forward.\nHe said, \"Listen to my words: When there are prophets of the Lord among you, I make myself known to them in visions or speak to them in dreams. But this is not the way I treat my servant Moses. He is the most faithful person in my household. **I speak with him face to face**, plainly and not in riddles. He even sees the form of the Lord. Why weren't you afraid to criticize my servant Moses?\" the Lord was angry with them, **so he left**.",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":220,
			"y":800,
			"width":740,
			"height":240
		},
		{"id":"7e14b626b3c027e9","type":"link","url":"https://youtu.be/JIMAqxGPR8Q?si=_jeTki5CxuuHT8Yb","x":-840,"y":-10,"width":400,"height":220}
	],
